NUM-29: average an N = 0 subarea's runoff over the whole step

A subarea with Manning's n = 0 releases its ponded depth in excess of
depression storage within the step. In the step in which depression storage
fills, getSubareaRunoff() turned that excess into a rate by dividing by
tRunoff, the time left after storage filled, while Voutflow and the
subcatchment runoff book the rate over the full step tStep. The water that
had just filled depression storage was therefore also counted as runoff.
Divide by tStep instead, so that rate x tStep is the excess volume.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-29_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
index 7c1d97c..30dbb73 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
@@ -1004,7 +1004,9 @@ double getSubareaRunoff(int j, int i, double area, double precip, double evap,
     }
 
     // --- compute runoff based on updated ponded depth
-    runoff = findSubareaRunoff(subarea, tRunoff);
+    //     (an N = 0 subarea's excess leaves within this step, so its
+    //     rate is averaged over the full step tStep, not over tRunoff)
+    runoff = findSubareaRunoff(subarea, tStep);
 
